  data: {
    LLM: "In a Small Game, try to void the suits where you have high cards as soon as possible. If you are void, you can discard your Kings and Aces into tricks won by others.\n\nBig Game Management: Only bid 'Big' if you have the Ace, Ten, and King of at least two suits, or a very long suit where you hold the top three cards. If you lose the lead, you lose the game.\n\nThe Overtake Trap: In a Small Game, if you are defending against the bidder, lead a suit where you know they have high cards. Because of the 'must-overtake' rule, you can force the bidder to win the trick with their Ace, causing them to fail their contract.",
    Player: "In a Small Game, try to void the suits where you have high cards as soon as possible. If you are void, you can discard your Kings and Aces into tricks won by others.\n\nBig Game Management: Only bid 'Big' if you have the Ace, Ten, and King of at least two suits, or a very long suit where you hold the top three cards. If you lose the lead, you lose the game.\n\nThe Overtake Trap: In a Small Game, if you are defending against the bidder, lead a suit where you know they have high cards. Because of the 'must-overtake' rule, you can force the bidder to win the trick with their Ace, causing them to fail their contract.",
    aggressiveness: 0.5,
    riskTolerance: 0.5,
    bluffFrequency: 0.3,
    bluffSettings: {
      profile: 'balanced',
    },
    basic: 'In a Small Game, try to void the suits where you have high cards as soon as possible. If you are void, you can discard your Kings and Aces into tricks won by others.',
    intermediate: "Big Game Management: Only bid 'Big' if you have the Ace, Ten, and King of at least two suits, or a very long suit where you hold the top three cards. If you lose the lead, you lose the game.",
    advanced: "The Overtake Trap: In a Small Game, if you are defending against the bidder, lead a suit where you know they have high cards. Because of the 'must-overtake' rule, you can force the bidder to win the trick with their Ace, causing them to fail their contract.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Count the cards! In a 32-card game, after 4 tricks, half the deck is gone. You should know exactly which cards are left for the end-play.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'If playing a Regular Game, avoid winning the 7th trick; the 8th trick often catches the player who had to lead it with unwanted face cards.',
      },
    ],
